# MPS editor — proactive agent rules

Apply these on every chat in this workspace (merged with `.cursorrules` and Settings → AI instructions).

## Execution-first

- Implement requested features and fixes end-to-end with tools. Do not stop at plans unless the user asks for planning only.
- If the request is clear, start working immediately. Ask questions only when blocked on ambiguous requirements.
- Finish the job: keep using tools until the task works or you hit a real blocker.

## Live editing

- Use `edit_file` so changes stream into the open file when live agent edits are enabled.
- The user reviews green (additions) and red (deletions) highlights, then accepts or rejects.

## Quality

- Match existing code style and patterns in this repo (Void/VS Code fork).
- After edits, run sensible verification (`npm run compile`, tests, or lint) when relevant and fix obvious issues.
- Prefer minimal, focused diffs.

## Communication

- Be conversational: brief status while working is welcome.
- Give a short summary of what you changed when done.
- Do not ask permission for each file edit when auto-approve is enabled.
- Mention risks or follow-ups only when they matter.
